# What must not travel to the build.
#
# `az acr build` uploads the whole context before anything is built, so what is
# listed here is the difference between a fast build and one that sends hundreds
# of megabytes of dependencies to be discarded on arrival.
#
# The image installs its own dependencies from the lockfiles, and anything
# already installed here was built for a different operating system anyway.
#
# Both forms of each pattern. The `**/` glob is not honoured identically by every
# builder, and a pattern that silently fails to match costs a hundred megabytes
# per deploy without ever reporting anything -- so the paths that actually exist
# are named as well.

# -- dependencies -------------------------------------------------------------
**/node_modules/
web/node_modules/

**/.venv/
**/venv/
mvstore/.venv/

# -- build output -------------------------------------------------------------
**/bin/
**/obj/
api/src/Counter.Api/bin/
api/src/Counter.Api/obj/
api/src/Counter.Domain/bin/
api/src/Counter.Domain/obj/
api/src/Counter.Infrastructure/bin/
api/src/Counter.Infrastructure/obj/
api/tests/Counter.UnitTests/bin/
api/tests/Counter.UnitTests/obj/
api/tests/Counter.IntegrationTests/bin/
api/tests/Counter.IntegrationTests/obj/
web/dist/

# -- caches -------------------------------------------------------------------
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
coverage/

# -- history, not source ------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.github/

# -- local run state ----------------------------------------------------------
.run/

# -- test artefacts -----------------------------------------------------------
web/cypress/videos/
web/cypress/screenshots/
web/cypress/downloads/

# -- secrets, and what a previous provision created ---------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
deploy/azure/environment.json

# -- the deployment's own definitions -----------------------------------------
# The image is built from a Dockerfile passed in by path; it does not need to
# contain its siblings.
deploy/
